# Keep every file byte-for-byte identical to what is committed.
# The engine sources contain legacy single-byte encodings (Windows-1252 /
# Latin-1) and must never be re-encoded or line-ending-normalized by any
# git client, whatever the local core.autocrlf setting is.
* -text

# cl_keys.cpp holds the localized key-name tables. The repository copy is
# UTF-8 so it stays valid for tools; git converts it to Windows-1252 on
# checkout and back to UTF-8 on checkin. The working tree therefore keeps
# the exact bytes the original engine source shipped (a single 0xDC byte
# for the Ue in RUECKTASTE, 0x93/0x94 for the curly quotes in the license
# header, etc.), and the compiled key-name strings stay identical to the
# original game. Editors must keep this file saved as Windows-1252, and
# checking out commits from before this rule existed can fail for this one
# file because those older blobs are not valid UTF-8.
code/client/cl_keys.cpp working-tree-encoding=WINDOWS-1252
